--[[
    LUNAR HUB - JNKIE key system  |  monochrome build
    Luau (Roblox), client-side, executor

    INLINE UI build, per https://docs.jnkie.com/roblox-sdk/inline-ui

    -- WHERE THIS GOES ---------------------------------------------------
    Dashboard -> Lua Scripts -> Lunar Hub -> UI-Source field.
    Your actual hub script stays in the Original Code field.
    Obfuscate this before pasting it in (the docs recommend Prometheus).

    This file only validates a key and opens the gate. It must never
    download the script itself - the public /download URL contains this
    same UI code, so fetching it here would relaunch the key prompt in a
    loop. That is the external-loader flow, and it is not this.

    -- LOGO --------------------------------------------------------------
    Three tiers, first one that works wins:
      1. CONFIG.LOGO_ASSET   - a rbxassetid:// string you uploaded
      2. CONFIG.LOGO_FILES   - a png in the executor workspace folder
      3. procedural          - crescent + L drawn from frames, always works

    -- HOW THE GATE WORKS ------------------------------------------------
    Junkie.check_key(key) makes a blocking HTTP call to the JNKIE backend:
      valid   -> { valid = true,  message = "KEY_VALID" | "KEYLESS" }
      invalid -> { valid = false, error   = "KEY_INVALID" | "http 429" | ... }
    On success the key goes into getgenv().SCRIPT_KEY. The while-loop at the
    bottom holds execution until that happens; once it releases, JNKIE runs
    your Original Code.
]]

